  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "A new place inside the line",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-24-0758-arc-2-ravi-teja-chilakala-enters-gold-as-cut-rises",
        "wire-2026-10-24-1756-arc-2-sakayori-lab-slips-out-of-gold"
      ],
      "text": "Ravi Teja Chilakala rises from 32nd to 13th against the previous close, adding 13.47 to reach 69.44. With the last of 16 provisional gold places now requiring 68.75, that leaves a cushion of 0.69. Sakayori Lab moves from 14th to 17th at an unchanged 68.06, also 0.69 from the boundary. Its fall shows the cost of standing still when challengers improve; it is not a score loss."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The leaders hold; fifth changes",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "Tufa Labs leads at 88.06, Yi-Chia Chen follows at 84.72 and nvbanana is third at 81.39, all unchanged against the previous close. Domdolus Tolus reaches fifth at 78.47 after an observed late score event from 73.47 and eighth place. Its previous-close comparison is unavailable, so the five-point event is not presented as its net daily gain. ARC Raiders holds the closing gold boundary at 16th with 68.75. The gold score line has risen 2.22 from the previous close. These are provisional public places; medals settle on the private board."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The rising line outpaces an early chase",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-24-0601-arc-2-gold-line-rises-enes-kulak-nears",
        "wire-2026-10-24-1004-arc-2-fukkatsu-surges-to-thirtieth",
        "wire-2026-10-24-1756-arc-2-fukkatsu-mixed-text-gains-thirteenth"
      ],
      "text": "The early wire put Enes Kulak 17th at 66.11 as the then-observed gold line reached 68.06. Later observations raised that line to 68.75. The earlier chase therefore does not establish that Kulak reached gold by the close. The same timing distinction matters for 復活の混テキスト: the daytime wire had it 30th at 58.33, while the closing report places it 31st at the same score. Its 13.89 gain is one improvement appearing in overlapping wire windows, not two separate advances."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Arcanio leads the next wave",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-24-1605-arc-2-laureano-arcanio-climbs-to-thirtieth",
        "wire-2026-10-24-1158-arc-2-cyrus-david-cao-enter-top-hundred"
      ],
      "text": "Laureano Arcanio adds 21.94 to reach 59.44, climbing from 74th to 30th against the previous close. Elsewhere, Shin & Maciej & Natalia reaches 22nd at 65.56 and nvnn 38th at 55.00. The afternoon wire recorded Cyrus at 94th with 35.42 and David Cao at 88th with 35.97; Cao closes 89th at the same score. ARC Mutants, the separate ARC2 entry, gains 2.50 to reach 41.81 and moves from 67th to 63rd."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The reporting boundary",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board"
      ],
      "text": "The field grows from 3,228 to 3,279 teams. Silver and bronze score lines remain 32.64 and 31.81. Social and discussion research was not refreshed for this edition; older public posts remain dated background. The standings show the gains and the pressure on medal places, without identifying the methods behind them."
    }
